Generated pages for this application land here, and wait here until they are
filed.

Filing one means moving it up into the application's folder, or into a band
inside it once the application grows enough to have bands. Folders do not affect
the build: every .vb under the project is compiled, RootNamespace is empty, and
each file declares its own namespace, so a page compiles wherever it sits.

The folders to avoid are the ones the project excludes - tests, project-backup
and restore-points. A page dropped in one of those leaves the build without
saying so.

Regenerating follows the file. PageGenerator looks the page up by name before it
writes, so a filed page is rewritten where it now lives and only a genuinely new
one is written here. Nothing remembers where a page came from.

This file exists because git does not track empty directories, and this folder is
empty whenever nothing is waiting - which is the state it should usually be in.
